@lang en
IMPORT `nd67-art12-13-claims`

-- Tests for Decree 67/2023/NĐ-CP, the compulsory motor insurance, both vintages.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the figures and percentages the SOURCE
-- prints, with the arithmetic written beside it, before the assertion was run. None was copied
-- from an evaluation. A failing assertion here is a finding, never a value to edit.
-- The per-row tests of Annex I and Annex VI are generated from the raw text, in
-- nd67-annex1-tests.l4 and nd67-annex6-tests.l4.
-- Kinds of number below: figures the source prints (150 million, 50 million, 100 million, the
-- Annex I and VI figures, 70/50/30/10/5/15%); and SCENARIO values chosen to make the arithmetic
-- visible (amounts of damage, agreed sums, dates, shares of fault), which are not law.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A vehicle, needing a licence or not.
GIVEN class   IS A `A vehicle class in Annex I`
      licence IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A motor vehicle`
`a vehicle of class` class `needing a licence` licence MEANS
    `A motor vehicle` WITH
        `class in Annex I`                                          IS class
        `beyond its service life under the law`                     IS FALSE
        `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
        `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year`  IS FALSE
        `subject to temporary registration`                         IS FALSE
        `a driving licence is required to drive it`                 IS licence

`a private car`        MEANS `a vehicle of class` (`a car not used for transport business` 5) `needing a licence` TRUE
`a motorbike`          MEANS `a vehicle of class` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 110) `needing a licence` TRUE
`an e-moped needing no licence` MEANS `a vehicle of class` `an electric moped` `needing a licence` FALSE

`a temporarily registered car` MEANS
    `A motor vehicle` WITH
        `class in Annex I`                                          IS `a car not used for transport business` 5
        `beyond its service life under the law`                     IS FALSE
        `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
        `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year`  IS FALSE
        `subject to temporary registration`                         IS TRUE
        `a driving licence is required to drive it`                 IS TRUE

-- A contract, from its dates.
GIVEN concluded IS A DATE
      begins    IS A DATE
      ends      IS A DATE
      vehicle   IS A `A motor vehicle`
      amended   IS A MAYBE `A vintage of Decree 67/2023`
      aligned   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
`a contract concluded on` concluded `running from` begins `to` ends `for` vehicle `amended to apply` amended `aligned to the owner's first contract` aligned MEANS
    `A contract of compulsory motor insurance` WITH
        `concluded on`                                     IS concluded
        `insurance begins on`                              IS begins
        `insurance ends on`                                IS ends
        `the premium paid`                                 IS 437000
        `the vehicle`                                      IS vehicle
        `amended by agreement to apply`                    IS amended
        `aligned with the owner's first contract of the year` IS aligned

GIVEN concluded IS A DATE
      vehicle   IS A `A motor vehicle`
GIVETH A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
`a one-year contract concluded on` concluded `for` vehicle MEANS
    `a contract concluded on` concluded `running from` concluded `to` (`add years` concluded 1) `for` vehicle `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE

-- The facts of an accident, named in a list. Every name used must be one of these (a test
-- below checks the fixtures), so a misspelt fact cannot silently read as false.
`the facts an accident fixture may name` MEANS
    LIST "not in traffic", "not moving", "uncontrolled", "owner handed the vehicle",
         "owner or driver intent", "fled", "fled but performed", "underage driver",
         "no licence", "invalid licence", "erased licence", "expired licence",
         "unmatched licence", "suspended licence", "alcohol", "drugs", "earthquake",
         "third party wholly at fault", "several vehicles"

GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every fact is known` facts MEANS
    all (GIVEN f YIELD elem f `the facts an accident fixture may name`) facts

GIVEN facts   IS A LIST OF STRING
      persons IS A LIST OF `A person harmed in the accident`
      share   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An accident`
`an accident where` facts `harming` persons `the owner's share of fault being` share MEANS
    `An accident` WITH
        `date of the accident`                                                         IS YMD 2026 8 3
        `the vehicle was participating in road traffic`                                 IS NOT (elem "not in traffic" facts)
        `the vehicle was moving, stopped or parked`                                     IS NOT (elem "not moving" facts)
        `the vehicle was under the control of its owner or a driver`                    IS NOT (elem "uncontrolled" facts)
        `the owner had handed possession and use of the vehicle to another`             IS elem "owner handed the vehicle" facts
        `the owner or the driver acted intentionally to cause the damage`              IS elem "owner or driver intent" facts
        `the driver who caused it deliberately fled`                                    IS elem "fled" facts
        `the driver who fled had performed the owner's civil liability`                 IS elem "fled but performed" facts
        `the driver did not meet the age condition of the Road Traffic Law`             IS elem "underage driver" facts
        `the driver had no driving licence`                                             IS elem "no licence" facts
        `the driver used an invalid driving licence`                                    IS elem "invalid licence" facts
        `the driver's licence was erased or altered`                                    IS elem "erased licence" facts
        `the driver's licence had expired at the time of the accident`                  IS elem "expired licence" facts
        `the driver used a licence not matching the vehicle`                            IS elem "unmatched licence" facts
        `the driver's right to use the licence was suspended for a term, or the licence was revoked` IS elem "suspended licence" facts
        `the driver's blood or breath alcohol exceeded the normal level in the Ministry of Health guidance` IS elem "alcohol" facts
        `the driver had used drugs or banned stimulants`                                IS elem "drugs" facts
        `caused by war, terrorism or an earthquake`                                     IS elem "earthquake" facts
        `an authority found it caused entirely by the fault of a third party`           IS elem "third party wholly at fault" facts
        `several motor vehicles caused it`                                              IS elem "several vehicles" facts
        `the owner's share of the fault`                                                IS share
        `the persons harmed`                                                            IS persons

GIVEN facts   IS A LIST OF STRING
      persons IS A LIST OF `A person harmed in the accident`
GIVETH AN `An accident`
`an accident where` facts `harming` persons MEANS
    `an accident where` facts `harming` persons `the owner's share of fault being` 1

-- Items of property.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      kind   IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `An item of damaged property`
`property worth` amount `that is` kind MEANS
    `An item of damaged property` WITH
        `the actual damage`                  IS amount
        `stolen or robbed in the accident`   IS kind EQUALS "stolen"
        `special property: gold, silver, precious stones, valuable papers such as money, antiques, rare paintings, a body or remains` IS kind EQUALS "gold"
        `an indirect consequence: loss of commercial value, or loss tied to the use and exploitation of the damaged property` IS kind EQUALS "indirect"

-- Injuries.
GIVEN key      IS A STRING
      item     IS A STRING
      assessed IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An injury`
`Annex VI item` key item `assessed at` assessed MEANS
    `an item of Annex VI` key item assessed NOTHING NOTHING FALSE

-- A person, by role. Roles: "driving", "on the vehicle", "passenger", "owner", "intent".
GIVEN roles    IS A LIST OF STRING
      died     IS A BOOLEAN
      injuries IS A LIST OF `An injury`
      property IS A LIST OF `An item of damaged property`
      agreed   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      court    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person harmed in the accident`
`a person who is` roles `dying` died `with injuries` injuries `and property` property `with an agreed sum of` agreed `and a court's sum of` court MEANS
    `A person harmed in the accident` WITH
        `driving the vehicle`                                     IS elem "driving" roles
        `on the vehicle`                                          IS elem "on the vehicle" roles
        `a passenger on the vehicle`                              IS elem "passenger" roles
        `the owner of the vehicle`                                IS elem "owner" roles
        `acted intentionally to cause the damage`                 IS elem "intent" roles
        `died`                                                    IS died
        `injuries`                                                IS injuries
        `damaged property`                                        IS property
        `amount agreed with the insured for health and life`      IS agreed
        `amount fixed by a court decision for health and life`    IS court
        `unidentified, or without a lawful heir`                  IS FALSE
        `actual necessary costs of burial and of keeping the remains to trace identity` IS 0

GIVEN roles    IS A LIST OF STRING
      died     IS A BOOLEAN
      injuries IS A LIST OF `An injury`
      property IS A LIST OF `An item of damaged property`
GIVETH A `A person harmed in the accident`
`a person who is` roles `dying` died `with injuries` injuries `and property` property MEANS
    `a person who is` roles `dying` died `with injuries` injuries `and property` property `with an agreed sum of` NOTHING `and a court's sum of` NOTHING

`a pedestrian killed`  MEANS `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY
`a passenger killed`   MEANS `a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle", "passenger") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY
`a pedestrian with a shoulder disarticulation` MEANS
    `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY

`no days off` MEANS `A working-day calendar` WITH `days off other than Saturdays and Sundays` IS EMPTY
`2 September 2026 off` MEANS `A working-day calendar` WITH `days off other than Saturdays and Sundays` IS LIST (YMD 2026 9 2)

§§ `The fixtures name only known facts`

#ASSERT `every fact is known` (LIST "not in traffic", "uncontrolled", "owner handed the vehicle", "owner or driver intent", "fled", "fled but performed", "underage driver", "no licence", "expired licence", "suspended licence", "alcohol", "drugs", "earthquake", "third party wholly at fault", "several vehicles")
#ASSERT NOT `every fact is known` (LIST "no licenses")

§§ `Which vintage governs: Article 76(1), 77(1); Decree 220 Article 10(1)-(2)`

-- Decree 67 from 6 September 2023; Decree 220 from 1 July 2026; the conclusion date decides.
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 9 5) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS `the rules Article 76(1) continues for a contract concluded before Decree 67/2023`
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 9 6) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS `Decree 67/2023, in the vintage` `Decree 67/2023 as made`
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS `Decree 67/2023, in the vintage` `Decree 67/2023 as made`
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS `Decree 67/2023, in the vintage` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`
-- Amended by agreement: a 2025 contract the parties bring under Decree 220; a 2023 contract they bring under Decree 67.
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `running from` (YMD 2025 12 1) `to` (YMD 2026 12 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` (JUST `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`) `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS `Decree 67/2023, in the vintage` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`
#ASSERT `the rules that govern` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 8 1) `running from` (YMD 2023 8 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` (JUST `Decree 67/2023 as made`) `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS `Decree 67/2023, in the vintage` `Decree 67/2023 as made`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the vintage that governs` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 9 5) `for` `a private car`)

§§ `Article 2(1), 3(1), 4`

#ASSERT `Article 3(1) — a vehicle owner` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(1) — a vehicle owner` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 2(1) — the decree applies, for the motor insurance, to the person` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) — the decree applies, for the motor insurance, to the person` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 4(1) — the person must buy the compulsory motor insurance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(3) — the insurer has separated the compulsory part as required` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 4(3) — the insurer has separated the compulsory part as required` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(5)(a) — the insurer may refuse to sell the insurance for` `a private car`
#ASSERT `Article 4(7) — the premium payment deadline is within the term` (YMD 2027 8 3) (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 8 3) `for` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(7) — the premium payment deadline is within the term` (YMD 2027 8 4) (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 8 3) `for` `a private car`)
#ASSERT `Article 4(8) — the compensation without what fraud added` 50000000 20000000 EQUALS 30000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the premium payment deadline the Minister of Finance sets is not encoded in this model`

§§ `Article 3(5)(a) — the third party, in both vintages`

-- src:nd220-2026-congbao-367 is quoted here for the term the second vintage uses:
-- src:nd220-2026-congbao-367:173 | 1. Thay thế cụm từ “người thứ ba” bằng cụm từ “bên thứ ba” tại khoản 5
-- src:nd220-2026-congbao-367:174 | Điều 3, Điều 5, điểm a khoản 1 Điều 7, điểm đ khoản 2 Điều 10, khoản 2 và
#ASSERT `the term for the third party in` `Decree 67/2023 as made` EQUALS "người thứ ba"
#ASSERT `the term for the third party in` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` EQUALS "bên thứ ba"
-- A pedestrian is a third party; the driver, a person on the vehicle, a passenger are not; the
-- owner is not, unless the owner had handed the vehicle to another. Same in both vintages.
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "driving", "on the vehicle") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` `a passenger killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "owner") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "owner") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` (LIST "owner handed the vehicle") `harming` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` (`a person who is` (LIST "owner") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` (LIST "owner handed the vehicle") `harming` EMPTY)

§§ `Article 6 — the limits`

#ASSERT `Article 6(1) — the limit for health and life, per person per accident` EQUALS 150000000
#ASSERT `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 110) EQUALS 50000000
#ASSERT `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` `an electric moped` EQUALS 50000000
#ASSERT `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` (`a car not used for transport business` 5) EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` `a tractor with its trailer` EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` (`a driving-school vehicle` (`a goods vehicle (truck)` 5)) EQUALS 100000000

§§ `Article 7 — scope, and each exclusion with a near miss`

-- Scope. In traffic: covered. Parked, unattended (not in traffic, not under control): outside.
-- Parked with the driver at the wheel (operating): covered.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "not in traffic", "uncontrolled") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `outside the scope: the vehicle was neither in road traffic nor operating`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "not in traffic") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
-- Passenger: health and life covered (7(1)(b)); property not.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a passenger killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a passenger killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "ordinary") (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `outside the scope: a passenger's property is not covered`
-- The driver: neither a third party nor a passenger.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "driving", "on the vehicle") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `outside the scope: the person is neither a third party nor a passenger`
-- (a) owner or driver intent; near miss: none.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "owner or driver intent") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: an intentional act of the owner or the driver`
-- (a) the injured person's intent excludes that person; near miss: another pedestrian.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "intent") `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` EMPTY) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: an intentional act of the injured person`
-- (b) fled without performing; near miss: fled but performed.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "fled") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: the driver fled without performing the owner's civil liability`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "fled", "fled but performed") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
-- (c) no licence for a car; near miss: no licence for an e-moped that needs none (reading (ii)).
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "no licence") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: the driver's age or licence`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "no licence") `harming` EMPTY) `an e-moped needing no licence` EQUALS `covered`
-- (c) under age, even on a vehicle needing no licence; expired; suspended (deemed none).
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "underage driver") `harming` EMPTY) `an e-moped needing no licence` EQUALS `excluded: the driver's age or licence`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "expired licence") `harming` EMPTY) `a motorbike` EQUALS `excluded: the driver's age or licence`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "suspended licence") `harming` EMPTY) `a motorbike` EQUALS `excluded: the driver's age or licence`
-- (d) an indirect consequence; near miss: the direct damage.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "indirect") (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: an indirect consequence`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "ordinary") (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
-- (đ) alcohol: property excluded; near miss: the same victim's life is covered.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "ordinary") (`an accident where` (LIST "alcohol") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: alcohol or drugs, for damage to property`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "alcohol") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `covered`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "ordinary") (`an accident where` (LIST "drugs") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: alcohol or drugs, for damage to property`
-- (e) stolen in the accident; (g) gold; near misses: ordinary property (above).
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "stolen") (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: property stolen or robbed in the accident`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for an item of property of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "gold") (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: special property`
-- (h) earthquake; near miss: none.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "earthquake") `harming` EMPTY) `a private car` EQUALS `excluded: war, terrorism or an earthquake`

§§ `Article 8 and Annex I — the premium of a contract (the per-row tests are generated)`

-- One year exactly: section A. Two years, 730 days: 437,000 / 365 x 730 = 874,000.
#ASSERT `Annex I — the premium for the term of` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS RIGHT 437000
#ASSERT `Annex I — the premium for the term of` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT 874000
-- 30 days or less: the annual premium / 12. 31 days: / 365 x 31.
#ASSERT `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 30 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000 EQUALS 437000 DIVIDED BY 12
#ASSERT `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 31 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000 EQUALS 437000 DIVIDED BY 365 TIMES 31
#ASSERT `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 1 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000 EQUALS 437000 DIVIDED BY 12
-- Article 8(2): at most 15% either way. 437,000 x 1.15 = 502,550; x 0.85 = 371,450.
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (15%) `to` 437000 EQUALS RIGHT 502550
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (0 MINUS 15%) `to` 437000 EQUALS RIGHT 371450
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (16%) `to` 437000 EQUALS LEFT `the premium adjustment exceeds 15% of the Annex I premium`
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (0 MINUS 16%) `to` 437000 EQUALS LEFT `the premium adjustment exceeds 15% of the Annex I premium`
-- Invalid classes.
#ASSERT `Annex I section A — the premium for a 1-year term, VAT not included, for` (`a car used for transport business` 0) EQUALS LEFT `a cylinder capacity, a number of seats or a payload is not a positive number`
#ASSERT `Annex I section A — the premium for a 1-year term, VAT not included, for` (`a driving-school vehicle` `a three-wheeled motorcycle`) EQUALS LEFT `the vehicle named for Annex I section VII.1 is not in section IV or VI`
-- The same premium in both vintages: contracts concluded the day before and the day Decree 220 took effect.
#ASSERT `the premium under the contract, after an adjustment of` 0 `for` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS RIGHT 437000
#ASSERT `the premium under the contract, after an adjustment of` 0 `for` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `for` `a private car`) EQUALS RIGHT 437000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the premium under the contract, after an adjustment of` 0 `for` (`a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 9 5) `for` `a private car`)

§§ `Article 9 — the term`

#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2027 1 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 12 31) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 12 31) `for` `a temporarily registered car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 7 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` TRUE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2029 1 1) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2029 1 2) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9 — the term is permitted for` (`a contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `running from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2025 12 31) `for` `a private car` `amended to apply` NOTHING `aligned to the owner's first contract` FALSE) EQUALS LEFT `the insurance ends before it begins`
#ASSERT `Article 9(3) — the former owner may terminate the contract` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11 states no refund for a termination on a change of owner, and this model does not invent one`

§§ `Article 10 — the certificate`

`a complete car certificate` MEANS
    `A certificate of insurance` WITH
        `(a) name, address and telephone number if any of the owner`               IS TRUE
        `(b) plate number, chassis number and engine number`                       IS TRUE
        `(c) for a car: type, payload, seats and purpose of use`                   IS TRUE
        `(d) name, address and hotline number of the insurer`                      IS TRUE
        `(dd) the limit of liability to third parties`                             IS TRUE
        `(e) the duties of the owner and the driver when an accident happens`      IS TRUE
        `(g) the term, the premium and the premium payment deadline`               IS TRUE
        `(h) the date of issue`                                                    IS TRUE
        `(i) a registered code and barcode identifying the insurer and the product` IS TRUE
        `issued for a car`                                                         IS TRUE

`a motorbike certificate without point (c)` MEANS
    `A certificate of insurance` WITH
        `(a) name, address and telephone number if any of the owner`               IS TRUE
        `(b) plate number, chassis number and engine number`                       IS TRUE
        `(c) for a car: type, payload, seats and purpose of use`                   IS FALSE
        `(d) name, address and hotline number of the insurer`                      IS TRUE
        `(dd) the limit of liability to third parties`                             IS TRUE
        `(e) the duties of the owner and the driver when an accident happens`      IS TRUE
        `(g) the term, the premium and the premium payment deadline`               IS TRUE
        `(h) the date of issue`                                                    IS TRUE
        `(i) a registered code and barcode identifying the insurer and the product` IS TRUE
        `issued for a car`                                                         IS FALSE

`a car certificate without the limit of liability` MEANS
    `A certificate of insurance` WITH
        `(a) name, address and telephone number if any of the owner`               IS TRUE
        `(b) plate number, chassis number and engine number`                       IS TRUE
        `(c) for a car: type, payload, seats and purpose of use`                   IS TRUE
        `(d) name, address and hotline number of the insurer`                      IS TRUE
        `(dd) the limit of liability to third parties`                             IS FALSE
        `(e) the duties of the owner and the driver when an accident happens`      IS TRUE
        `(g) the term, the premium and the premium payment deadline`               IS TRUE
        `(h) the date of issue`                                                    IS TRUE
        `(i) a registered code and barcode identifying the insurer and the product` IS TRUE
        `issued for a car`                                                         IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Article 10(2) — the certificate carries every particular it must` `a complete car certificate`
#ASSERT `Article 10(2) — the certificate carries every particular it must` `a motorbike certificate without point (c)`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10(2) — the certificate carries every particular it must` `a car certificate without the limit of liability`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10(3) — the electronic certificate is valid` `a complete car certificate` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10(1) — one certificate for the vehicle` 1
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10(1) — one certificate for the vehicle` 2

