§§ `Article 12(3) — the advance, its percentages and its deadline`

-- (a) found within the scope: death, 70% of an estimated 150,000,000 = 105,000,000; a partial
-- injury, 50% of an estimated 30,000,000 = 15,000,000; a vegetative state (Part B I.4.1), 50%.
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` TRUE `death` `on an estimated compensation of` 150000000 EQUALS `an advance of` 105000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` TRUE (`a partial injury` 20) `on an estimated compensation of` 30000000 EQUALS `an advance of` 15000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` TRUE `a brain injury leaving a persistent vegetative state` `on an estimated compensation of` 150000000 EQUALS `an advance of` 75000000
-- (b) not yet found: 30% of 150,000,000 = 45,000,000 for a death or an estimate of 81% or more;
-- 10% = 15,000,000 for 31% to under 81%; nothing listed under 31%.
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE `death` `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `an advance of` 45000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE (`a partial injury` 81) `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `an advance of` 45000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE (`a partial injury` 80.9) `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `an advance of` 15000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE (`a partial injury` 31) `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `an advance of` 15000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE (`a partial injury` 30.9) `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `none of the cases Article 12(3) lists`
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the advance for` FALSE `a brain injury leaving a persistent vegetative state` `on an estimated compensation of` 0 EQUALS `an advance of` 45000000
-- The deadline: 3 working days. Notice on Monday 5 October 2026: last day Thursday 8 October.
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — under` `no days off` `the last day for the advance, notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 8
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — under` `no days off` `an advance paid on` (YMD 2026 10 8) `for a notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `is in time`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 12(3) — under` `no days off` `an advance paid on` (YMD 2026 10 9) `for a notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `is in time`
-- Notice on Friday 2 October: Monday 5, Tuesday 6, Wednesday 7.
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — under` `no days off` `the last day for the advance, notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 7
-- Notice on Tuesday 1 September, 2 September a day off (a scenario calendar): 3, 4 and 7 September.
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — under` `2 September 2026 off` `the last day for the advance, notice received on` (YMD 2026 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 7
#ASSERT `Article 12(3) — the insurer may ask the Fund to repay the advance` TRUE

§§ `Article 12(4) and (7) — 5 working days, and up to 5%`

-- Accident on Monday 5 October 2026: 6, 7, 8, 9 and 12 October.
#ASSERT `Article 12(4) — under` `no days off` `the last day for the written notice, accident on` (YMD 2026 10 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 12
#ASSERT `Article 12(4) — under` `no days off` `a written notice sent on` (YMD 2026 10 12) `for an accident on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `is in time, given force majeure` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 12(4) — under` `no days off` `a written notice sent on` (YMD 2026 10 13) `for an accident on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `is in time, given force majeure` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 12(4) — under` `no days off` `a written notice sent on` (YMD 2026 10 20) `for an accident on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `is in time, given force majeure` TRUE
-- 12(7): 30,000,000 for property; 5% off = 28,500,000; 5.01% is too much; no ground, no reduction.
#ASSERT `Article 12(7) — the compensation for property after a reduction of` (5%) `from` 30000000 `where the notice was not sent` TRUE `or a change was not notified` FALSE EQUALS RIGHT 28500000
#ASSERT `Article 12(7) — the compensation for property after a reduction of` (5.01%) `from` 30000000 `where the notice was not sent` TRUE `or a change was not notified` FALSE EQUALS LEFT `the reduction exceeds 5% of the compensation for property`
#ASSERT `Article 12(7) — the compensation for property after a reduction of` (3%) `from` 30000000 `where the notice was not sent` FALSE `or a change was not notified` FALSE EQUALS LEFT `Article 12(7) gives no ground for a reduction`
#ASSERT `Article 12(7) — the compensation for property after a reduction of` (3%) `from` 30000000 `where the notice was not sent` FALSE `or a change was not notified` TRUE EQUALS RIGHT 29100000
#ASSERT `Article 12(7) — the compensation for property after a reduction of` 0 `from` 30000000 `where the notice was not sent` FALSE `or a change was not notified` FALSE EQUALS RIGHT 30000000

§§ `Article 12(5) — who is paid`

#ASSERT `Article 12(5) — the insurer pays` FALSE EQUALS `the insurance buyer or the insured`
#ASSERT `Article 12(5) — the insurer pays` TRUE EQUALS `the injured person`

§§ `Article 12(6)(a) and Annex VI — health and life`

-- Death: Part A, 100% of 150,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 150000000
-- B.VI 1.4, shoulder disarticulation, 72%: 108,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian with a shoulder disarticulation` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 108000000
-- B.I 1.1 (6-10%), assessed at 8%: 12,000,000. Assessed at 11%: outside the band. Not assessed: declined.
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.I" "1.1" `assessed at` (JUST 8))) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 12000000
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.I" "1.1" `assessed at` (JUST 11))) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS LEFT `the assessed rate lies outside the band of the item`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.I" "1.1" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY)
-- No such item; a heading.
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.I" "99" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS LEFT `the item is not in Annex VI`
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.I" "1" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS LEFT `the item fixes no rate of its own`
-- Special case 4: 72% + 1.5% (B.IX 2.1.1) = 73.5% = 110,250,000; 72% + 72% (B.VI 6.3) = 144%, held at 150,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING), (`Annex VI item` "B.IX" "2.1.1" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 110250000
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING), (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "6.3" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 150000000
-- The note on items 4.2.9-4.2.16 of section I: B.I 4.2.13 (21-25%): upper limb 25% = 37,500,000; lower 21% = 31,500,000.
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`an item of Annex VI` "B.I" "4.2.13" NOTHING (JUST `an upper limb`) NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT 25
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`an item of Annex VI` "B.I" "4.2.13" NOTHING (JUST `a lower limb`) NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT 21
-- The note on items 6.3.7-6.3.8: B.I 6.3.7 (5-9%): a woman 9%, a man 5%.
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`an item of Annex VI` "B.I" "6.3.7" NOTHING NOTHING (JUST `female`) FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT 9
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`an item of Annex VI` "B.I" "6.3.7" NOTHING NOTHING (JUST `male`) FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT 5
-- A row whose addition (cộng lùi) applies: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`an item of Annex VI` "B.X" "2.6.3" (JUST 38) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE)
-- The acuity table: one eye at 1/10, the other with no light perception: 71%, either way round.
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`reduced visual acuity of both eyes, by the acuity table` `1/10` `no light perception`) EQUALS RIGHT 71
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`reduced visual acuity of both eyes, by the acuity table` `no light perception` `1/10`) EQUALS RIGHT 71
-- Special case 1: stiffness of the middle finger, 50% of the loss of it (B.VI 4.5.3.6, 8-10%, assessed 10%): 5%.
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`stiffness of the joints of a digit, special case 1` FALSE "B.VI" "4.5.3.6" (JUST 10)) EQUALS RIGHT 5
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`stiffness of the joints of a digit, special case 1` TRUE "B.VI" "4.5.1.5" (JUST 25)) EQUALS LEFT `special case 1 does not apply to a thumb, an index finger or a big toe`
-- Special case 3: the only eye lost, as both eyes (B.VIII 1.4, 87%).
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` `the loss of the only remaining eye, special case 3` EQUALS RIGHT 87
-- Special case 5: an unlisted injury rated 20% = 30,000,000; unrated, declined.
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`an injury not listed in Annex VI, special case 5` (JUST 20))) `and property` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 30000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Annex VI amount for` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`an injury not listed in Annex VI, special case 5` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY)
-- Agreement and court (12(6)(a)): agreed 80,000,000 under the 108,000,000 of B.VI 1.4: 80,000,000.
-- Agreed 120,000,000: held at 108,000,000. A court's 90,000,000 prevails over an agreement: 90,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY `with an agreed sum of` (JUST 80000000) `and a court's sum of` NOTHING) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 80000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY `with an agreed sum of` (JUST 120000000) `and a court's sum of` NOTHING) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 108000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY `with an agreed sum of` (JUST 80000000) `and a court's sum of` (JUST 90000000)) (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 90000000
-- Entirely a third party's fault: a third party gets 50%: 75,000,000 for a death; a passenger, 100%.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "third party wholly at fault") `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 75000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "third party wholly at fault") `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 75000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a passenger killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "third party wholly at fault") `harming` EMPTY) EQUALS RIGHT 150000000
-- Several vehicles, the owner's share of the fault 0.6: 60% of 150,000,000 = 90,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "several vehicles") `harming` EMPTY `the owner's share of fault being` 0.6) EQUALS RIGHT 90000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` `a pedestrian killed` (`an accident where` (LIST "several vehicles") `harming` EMPTY `the owner's share of fault being` 1.2) EQUALS LEFT `a share of fault is not between 0 and 1`
-- Special case 6: unidentified dead; burial costs 20,000,000, paid; 200,000,000, held at the limit.
`an unidentified victim whose burial cost` MEANS
    `A person harmed in the accident` WITH
        `driving the vehicle`                                     IS FALSE
        `on the vehicle`                                          IS FALSE
        `a passenger on the vehicle`                              IS FALSE
        `the owner of the vehicle`                                IS FALSE
        `acted intentionally to cause the damage`                 IS FALSE
        `died`                                                    IS TRUE
        `injuries`                                                IS EMPTY
        `damaged property`                                        IS EMPTY
        `amount agreed with the insured for health and life`      IS NOTHING
        `amount fixed by a court decision for health and life`    IS NOTHING
        `unidentified, or without a lawful heir`                  IS TRUE
        `actual necessary costs of burial and of keeping the remains to trace identity` IS 20000000
#ASSERT `the Annex VI amount for` `an unidentified victim whose burial cost` EQUALS RIGHT 20000000

§§ `Article 12(6)(b) — property, per accident`

-- A car (limit 100,000,000): two third parties' property, 30,000,000 + 40,000,000 = 70,000,000.
`a pedestrian with property` MEANS `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` (LIST (`property worth` 30000000 `that is` "ordinary"), (`property worth` 40000000 `that is` "ordinary"))
`a cyclist with property` MEANS `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` (LIST (`property worth` 50000000 `that is` "ordinary"))
`a pedestrian with stolen and golden property` MEANS `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` FALSE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` (LIST (`property worth` 30000000 `that is` "ordinary"), (`property worth` 10000000 `that is` "stolen"), (`property worth` 5000000 `that is` "gold"), (`property worth` 7000000 `that is` "indirect"))
`a passenger with luggage` MEANS `a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle", "passenger") `dying` FALSE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` (LIST (`property worth` 20000000 `that is` "ordinary"))
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with property`)) `a private car` EQUALS RIGHT 70000000
-- + a cyclist's 50,000,000 = 120,000,000: held at the car's 100,000,000; a motorbike's limit is 50,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with property`, `a cyclist with property`)) `a private car` EQUALS RIGHT 100000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with property`)) `a motorbike` EQUALS RIGHT 50000000
-- The owner's share of the fault 0.5: 35,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with property`) `the owner's share of fault being` 0.5) `a private car` EQUALS RIGHT 35000000
-- Excluded items drop out: only the 30,000,000 of ordinary property counts; a passenger's luggage does not.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` EMPTY `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with stolen and golden property`, `a passenger with luggage`)) `a private car` EQUALS RIGHT 30000000
-- Alcohol: no property at all, while the same accident's deaths are paid.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(b) — the compensation for property in the accident` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`an accident where` (LIST "alcohol") `harming` (LIST `a pedestrian with property`)) `a private car` EQUALS RIGHT 0

§§ `Article 12(9) — the first contract pays`

`contract A, concluded 10 January` MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `for` `a private car`
`contract B, concluded 1 February`  MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 2 1)  `for` `a private car`
`contract C, also concluded 10 January` MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `for` `a private car`
#ASSERT `Article 12(9) — what becomes of` `contract A, concluded 10 January` `among` (LIST `contract A, concluded 10 January`, `contract B, concluded 1 February`) EQUALS `this is the contract that pays`
#ASSERT `Article 12(9) — what becomes of` `contract B, concluded 1 February` `among` (LIST `contract A, concluded 10 January`, `contract B, concluded 1 February`) EQUALS `this contract does not pay, and its premium is refunded in full` 437000
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 12(9) — what becomes of` `contract A, concluded 10 January` `among` (LIST `contract A, concluded 10 January`, `contract C, also concluded 10 January`)

§§ `Article 13 — the claim file`

`a complete file` MEANS
    `A claim file` WITH
        `(1) the written request for compensation`                                    IS TRUE
        `(2)(a) the vehicle registration certificate, or a document Article 13(2)(a) accepts instead` IS TRUE
        `(2)(b) the driving licence`                                                   IS TRUE
        `(2)(c) the driver's identity card, citizen identity card, passport or other identity paper` IS TRUE
        `(2)(d) the insurance certificate`                                             IS TRUE
        `(3)(a) the injury certificate`                                                IS TRUE
        `(3)(b) the medical record`                                                    IS TRUE
        `(3)(c) the death extract, death notice, police confirmation or forensic result` IS TRUE
        `(4)(a) invoices, vouchers or evidence of the repair or replacement`           IS TRUE
        `(4)(b) papers on the costs the owner incurred to limit the loss or on the insurer's instructions` IS TRUE
        `(5) the police documents on the accident`                                     IS TRUE
        `(6) the insurer's assessment record`                                          IS TRUE
        `(7) the court decision`                                                       IS TRUE

`a file with no licence and no police documents` MEANS
    `A claim file` WITH
        `(1) the written request for compensation`                                    IS TRUE
        `(2)(a) the vehicle registration certificate, or a document Article 13(2)(a) accepts instead` IS TRUE
        `(2)(b) the driving licence`                                                   IS FALSE
        `(2)(c) the driver's identity card, citizen identity card, passport or other identity paper` IS TRUE
        `(2)(d) the insurance certificate`                                             IS TRUE
        `(3)(a) the injury certificate`                                                IS FALSE
        `(3)(b) the medical record`                                                    IS FALSE
        `(3)(c) the death extract, death notice, police confirmation or forensic result` IS TRUE
        `(4)(a) invoices, vouchers or evidence of the repair or replacement`           IS FALSE
        `(4)(b) papers on the costs the owner incurred to limit the loss or on the insurer's instructions` IS FALSE
        `(5) the police documents on the accident`                                     IS FALSE
        `(6) the insurer's assessment record`                                          IS TRUE
        `(7) the court decision`                                                       IS FALSE

`a claim for a third party's death` MEANS
    `A kind of claim` WITH
        `for harm to health or life`                                                   IS TRUE
        `a victim died`                                                                IS TRUE
        `for damage to property`                                                       IS FALSE
        `a third party or a passenger died, or it must be verified that the accident was entirely a third party's fault` IS TRUE
        `a court decision exists`                                                      IS FALSE
        `the insurer repaired or made good the damage itself`                          IS FALSE
        `the owner incurred costs to limit the loss or on the insurer's instructions`  IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Article 13 — the documents the buyer or insured has still to gather` `a claim for a third party's death` `a private car` `a complete file` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Article 13 — the documents the buyer or insured has still to gather` `a claim for a third party's death` `a private car` `a file with no licence and no police documents` EQUALS LIST "(2)(b) the driving licence"
#ASSERT `Article 13 — the documents the buyer or insured has still to gather` `a claim for a third party's death` `an e-moped needing no licence` `a file with no licence and no police documents` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Article 13 — the documents the insurer has still to gather` `a claim for a third party's death` `a file with no licence and no police documents` EQUALS LIST "(5) the police documents on the accident"

§§ `One scenario through every layer, in both vintages`

-- A car, a contract concluded the day before or the day Decree 220 took effect; an accident in
-- traffic in which the driver had drunk; a pedestrian killed carrying 30,000,000 + 40,000,000
-- of property; a passenger with a shoulder disarticulation (B.VI 1.4, 72%).
-- Cover: the pedestrian's life and the passenger's health are covered; the property is excluded
-- by Article 7(2)(đ). Amounts: 150,000,000 for the death, 108,000,000 for the passenger, 0 for
-- property. Both vintages give the same answers; a contract concluded before Decree 67 is declined.
`the pedestrian, killed with property` MEANS `a person who is` EMPTY `dying` TRUE `with injuries` EMPTY `and property` (LIST (`property worth` 30000000 `that is` "ordinary"), (`property worth` 40000000 `that is` "ordinary"))
`the passenger, shoulder lost` MEANS `a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle", "passenger") `dying` FALSE `with injuries` (LIST (`Annex VI item` "B.VI" "1.4" `assessed at` NOTHING)) `and property` EMPTY
`the drink-driving accident` MEANS `an accident where` (LIST "alcohol") `harming` (LIST `the pedestrian, killed with property`, `the passenger, shoulder lost`)
`the contract of 30 June 2026` MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `for` `a private car`
`the contract of 1 July 2026`  MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `for` `a private car`
`the contract of 5 September 2023` MEANS `a one-year contract concluded on` (YMD 2023 9 5) `for` `a private car`

